    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Normalized Ancestry Feat.</strong> Formerly granted automatically by <em>Human (Florensis)</em> at level 17; now available as an optional ancestry feat.</p><p><em>“People tell stories about you and then you do THIS to them.”</em></p><p><strong>Living Folklore (1/Long Rest).</strong> For 1 minute, you can’t be targeted by opportunity attacks, and once per turn you can force an enemy’s attack to miss you (reaction) by “being somewhere else in the story.”</p>",
